<title>USA: Hilton acquires southern Calif. hotel.</title>
<headline>Hilton acquires southern Calif. hotel.</headline>
<dateline>BEVERLY HILLS, Calif. 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hilton Hotels Corp said Monday it has acquired the 371-room Torrance Hilton at South Bay in Torrance, Calif., a suburb of Los Angeles.</p>
<p>Financial details were undisclosed.</p>
<p>The 12-story hotel had been an independently owned franchise. It has 15,000 square feet of meeting space that can hold up to 500 people.</p>
<p>A $10 million renovation on all guest rooms, 34 suites, the lobby and meeting space was completed in September.</p>
<p>Hilton now has 34 hotels in California with roughly 14,300 rooms.</p>
</text>
